# CR 508.3a, 603.2c, 406.3, 607.2a. Connecting the Dots exiles the top card of its controller's library face down for each
# creature that attacks, and sacrificing it (with its hand discarded) puts every card exiled with it into its owner's hand.
#
# Turn 1: Mox Pearl pays for Mother of Runes. Turn 3: Connecting the Dots is cast, and Mother of Runes attacks, so Ancestral
# Recall, the top card of the library after the turn's draw, goes into exile face down: the dump lists it as "(face down)"
# and Exile.FaceDown, the omniscient view, says what it is. Turn 5: the enchantment is sacrificed for {1}{R} and the hand
# (three Islands and the Lightning Bolt drawn on turn 3) is discarded; Ancestral Recall comes back into the hand.

